  "public_messages": [
    "I’ll read the project instructions, build the application, and verify the API, browser workflow, persistence, and performance locally.\n",
    "I’m using Python’s standard library, SQLite, and a plain JavaScript frontend. This keeps startup dependency-free. Stock changes, order transitions, audit events, and retry records will commit in one transaction so concurrent requests and restarts preserve the same guarantees.\n",
    "The API and transaction layer are in place. Tenant access comes from the authenticated session, and retry records are stored with the changes they protect. Next I’m building the operator workflow, including forms that retain input after validation or stale-version errors.\n",
    "The frontend now supports order creation, fulfillment, returns, stock adjustments, and audit browsing. API tests are running against real server processes and SQLite files, including concurrent requests and rejected operations. I’m adding browser checks and an isolated load script next.\n",
    "All 13 API integration tests passed, including concurrent reservations, identical retries, tenant isolation, and restart durability. The browser run passed the fulfillment and stale-input workflows before hitting a timing issue in the test’s filter assertion. I’m correcting that wait, then finishing the mobile and role checks.\n",
    "The browser workflow now passes on desktop and at 390px, including viewer access, tenant separation, safe text rendering, and retrying a lost response without duplicating an order. I also reviewed the screenshots and am improving the mobile return form so its inputs are visible without horizontal scrolling.\n",
    "I strengthened pagination so a filtered list keeps its original matching orders even if their statuses change between pages. The larger load run exposed client-side TCP port exhaustion from opening a connection for every request. The workload now reuses HTTP/1.1 connections per worker, and I’m rerunning it at one and eight concurrent workers.\n",
    "Both load runs completed without HTTP errors or stock/audit mismatches: each exercised 8,000 writes and 10,000 reads. At eight workers, writes reached about 2,330 requests/sec, with a 50 ms p99 and a 1.4-second maximum. Reads were slower at eight workers than at one; I’m recording those limits alongside the results.\n",
    "The deliverables and verification are complete. The final run passed 15 API tests and 11 browser scenarios, including process-kill recovery and rapid double submission. Setup instructions, architecture notes, screenshots, performance results, and limitations are recorded; `TASK.md` and `TOOLING.md` are unchanged.\n",
    "Built DepotFlow with a persistent SQLite backend, complete frontend, tenant/role isolation, atomic stock operations, durable retries, and audit history.\n\nRun:\n\n```sh\nPORT=8000 DATA_DIR=\"$PWD/.data\" SEED_DEMO=1 ./run.sh\n```\n\nOpen http://127.0.0.1:8000. Sign in as `admin@north.example` using `DepotDemo!2026`.\n\nVerification passed: **15 API tests, 11 browser scenarios, and 36,000 measured requests with zero errors**.\n\nSetup, design, commands, measurements, and limitations are documented in `README.md`, `architecture.md`, and `evidence/`. `TASK.md` and `TOOLING.md` were preserved."
  ],
  "final": "Built DepotFlow with a persistent SQLite backend, complete frontend, tenant/role isolation, atomic stock operations, durable retries, and audit history.\n\nRun:\n\n```sh\nPORT=8000 DATA_DIR=\"$PWD/.data\" SEED_DEMO=1 ./run.sh\n```\n\nOpen http://127.0.0.1:8000. Sign in as `admin@north.example` using `DepotDemo!2026`.\n\nVerification passed: **15 API tests, 11 browser scenarios, and 36,000 measured requests with zero errors**.\n\nSetup, design, commands, measurements, and limitations are documented in `README.md`, `architecture.md`, and `evidence/`. `TASK.md` and `TOOLING.md` were preserved.",
